      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really moving piece, it definitely touches on that feeling of loss people are describing.\n\ni'm just wondering how to handle the critics though. i know there are going to be people reading this who will immediately get defensive. they'll say that focusing on \"shared roots\" and \"tradition\" is just a thinly veiled way to stay closed off to new people and different backgrounds. \n\nthey'll argue that what we're calling \"social glue\" is actually just a barrier to entry that makes it impossible for anyone who didn't grow up here to ever truly belong. how can we address that in the article? how can we make it clear that we're talking about the strength of the community itself, and not just a way to keep people out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
